This crate (`symphonia-codec-cook`) is a pure-Rust RealAudio Cook decoder. It is licensed under the
Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0, like the rest of Project Symphonia.

Cook has no public specification. The bitstream parsing, bit allocation (`categorize`), vector
dequantisation, joint-stereo decoupling, MLT windowing and gain-control logic follow FFmpeg's
`libavcodec/cook.c`, and the Huffman and scale tables (`src/tables.rs`, extracted programmatically)
come from `libavcodec/cookdata.h`. The additive lagged-Fibonacci noise generator follows
`libavutil/lfg.c`. These files are distributed under the GNU Lesser General Public License,
version 2.1 or later.

